   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Structure and meaning of the Zustandspassiv",
     "texto": [
      "While the process passive with **werden** highlights the development of the action, the stative passive with **sein** presents the static condition reached after that action has ended: **Die Tür ist geschlossen** (the door is closed) versus **Die Tür wird geschlossen** (someone is closing the door).",
      "In the technical field and quality control, the Zustandspassiv is the usual format for confirming completed protocols and checks: **Das System ist kalibriert** (the system is calibrated), **Die Schutzkleidung ist angelegt** (the protective clothing is put on)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Aspect",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Vorgangspassiv (werden)",
       "lengua": "estudio"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Zustandspassiv (sein)",
       "lengua": "estudio"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "Focus",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "The action or the process in progress",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "The result or stationary state",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Present",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Das Ventil wird geöffnet. (it opens)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Das Ventil ist geöffnet. (is open)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Past",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Das Ventil wurde geöffnet. (it was opened)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Das Ventil war geöffnet. (it was open)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
